  "version": 1,
  "notes": "AzCrash Baseline1: built from SPEAR captures (Bell V1-V1, Bow V1-V2, Edge V1-V3; bow and bell with the stick tip, edge with the shoulder) by build_preset.py: 900-mode bank from bow and edge partials (0.3 % clusters; exc from the bow captures only, 80th-percentile presence, gamma 0.8, <400 Hz x0.65), decay-fitted T60 calibrated per band to the SPEAR band decay (t60_scale 1.0), NPZ edge in the plugin's 22 bands with edge_rms_correction from the velw norms. Build-up as Bettis/Swish. Then calibrated by rendering the plugin against the recordings the captures came from (2026-11-22, Kris): mode exc, T60 and bell ratios per range against BeadSoft, BeadMedium and BellSoft; the edge rows against CrashSoft, CrashMedium and CrashLoud (one set of mode weights, each row's band envelopes matched per band and time window, the modes below 112 Hz weighted from the SPEAR energy near them). See docs/BASELINE_MANIFEST.md."
